          "<p>The same functionality can require different amounts of code in different languages. <b>LOC is language-dependent; FP measures user-level functionality independently of implementation technology.</b></p><p>Agree whether comments, blank lines or executable statements count before comparing LOC. KLOC means a thousand lines: 22,500 LOC = 22.5 KLOC.</p><div class=\"callout warn\">“LOC is independent of programming language” is false. Give the language dependence as your reason.</div>",
