          "<p>The figure labels each task with its duration in weeks. Task 4 needs both 2 and 3; task 8 needs both 5 and 7.</p><p><b>TE = max(predecessor TE) + own duration</b>, where TE is earliest completion.</p><ol><li>TE1=5; TE2=9; TE3=11.</li><li>TE4=max(9,11)+2=13.</li><li>TE5=18.5; TE6=18; TE7=21.</li><li>TE8=max(18.5,21)+1=<b>22 weeks</b>.</li></ol><div class=\"callout warn\">At a merge take the maximum predecessor completion, then add the current duration. Do not sum the branches.</div>",
